"settings.data.explanation" = "The documented account/usage/read method is used for aggregate reconciliation. The application does not enable experimental app-server APIs. Model and input/output/cache details come from token_count in local history. The session-file schema is not a stable public contract, so this layer is marked experimental.";
"settings.otel.explanation" = "The receiver accepts JSON only at 127.0.0.1:4319/v1/logs. The proposed configuration sets log_user_prompt=false. Restart Codex completely after adding it. No keys or auth.json are read.";
"settings.import.schema" = "Each record must contain timestamp, model, input_tokens, and output_tokens. Optional fields: cached_input_tokens, cache_write_tokens, and source. JSON may be an array or a {\"records\": [...]} object; JSONL uses one object per line.";
"settings.import.otelSchema" = "OTel JSONL import recognizes common gen_ai.usage.* fields and OTLP attributes. The exact JSON shape depends on the selected OpenTelemetry Collector/exporter, so the normalized format above remains the recommended contract.";
"settings.privacy.local" = "The application stores imported usage records and the pricing table only locally in Application Support.";
"settings.privacy.sessions" = "Only model settings and token_count are read from session files; message text, tool calls, and auth.json are ignored.";
"settings.pricing.subtitle" = "Rates in USD per 1 million tokens. A trailing `*` in a pattern denotes a prefix.";
"settings.about.purpose" = "The application provides a personal estimate of Codex work in tokens and its approximate equivalent at public API prices.";
"settings.about.realNumbers" = "Codex app-server provides the documented account/usage/read method with aggregate tokens and daily buckets for Codex-backed authentication. The application uses only the stable protocol surface and does not enable experimental APIs. Model and input/output/cache breakdowns come from local token_count events and, when configured, the documented OTel response.completed event. Local rollout files are used as an experimental backfill and may change between Codex versions.";
